"g009|Matchstick Bridge|Puzzle / Engineering|js|drag|paper|Drag matchsticks to bridge a gap, then press test and watch it either hold or humiliate you.|Build with a fixed number of sticks under a weight limit, then commit to the load test.|The sticks are physics bodies, so a bridge that looks right but is triangulated wrong will fold in a satisfying way.|Levels are generated by width, stick budget and load, with a solver checking that at least one valid bridge exists.|The test button converts a quiet building game into a moment of genuine suspense.|puzzle,physics,building,levels",

"g010|Domino Drift|Arcade / Physics|js|drag|vector|Place dominoes with your finger, then tap once and watch the wave travel.|You have a limited set of dominoes per level. Lay them to topple through every target in one chain.|Domino spacing tolerance is tight, so placement is the skill and the topple is the payoff.|Endless: generator produces target layouts in new shapes (spirals, branches, splits) with shrinking tile budgets.|The single-tap payoff after careful placement is a compressed build-and-release loop that ends in a satisfying cascade.|physics,building,cascade,planning",

